					]
				}
			],
			"disabled": true
		},
		{
			"id": "tAHQNknLlGMIuWsyP",
			"name": "Lost to the Path",
			"reference": "B136",
			"local_notes": "As Fanaticism (single-minded devotion to one specific cause — here, the Path itself), but the \"cause\" is a role rather than a belief: an Exarch cannot set the Warrior mantle down and walk away as an ordinary Aspect Warrior does when their years in the shrine end, and a Farseer cannot un-see the futures they have learned to read. Apply to Exarch and Farseer characters specifically.\n\nLore: Both Codex background and the Path trilogy are explicit that some Aeldari, having walked one Path far enough, are lost to it permanently — an Exarch fuses, in a very real sense, with their shrine's war spirit and the ancient armour they don to lead it; a Farseer's mind is so given over to prophecy that an ordinary life is no longer available to them. It is treated as an honour and a tragedy in equal measure, never a punishment.\n\nDesign: Fanaticism (B136, -15 points): a psychological grip strong enough that the character will not, and increasingly cannot, walk away from the Path's demands, exactly Fanaticism's own definition, redirected from a belief system onto the Path itself.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "TAzUbcT2T1ypwsagv",
			"name": "Aspect Training",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What a Shrine actually does to a Guardian who commits to the Path of the Warrior: years, sometimes decades, of drilling one narrow art of war until body and reflex both match its demands — matching framework.md's own note that this is exactly what closes the gap to a Space Marine's DX.\n\nDesign: 75 (Attribute Modifiers) + 15 (Enhanced Dodge 1) = 90 points, added to the Aeldari Physiology + Keen Battle-Sense baseline (154 + 5 = 159) for 249 points of physiology before skills. See the Aspect Warrior template for the full character, and Exarch's Mastery below for the further step up to Exarch.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tdSNUQ8t-IGAn6uz_",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Aspect Training)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target over the Aeldari Physiology + Keen Battle-Sense baseline: ST 11, DX 16, IQ 12 (unchanged), HT 11, Will 13, Per 13 (unchanged, already delivered by Keen Battle-Sense at this IQ). Increased ST +1 (B14, 10/level, 10) for ST 11 — enough muscle to wear Aspect armour and carry a fusion gun or exarch blade, nowhere near an Astartes' bulk. Increased DX +2 (B15, 20/level, 40) for DX 16, matching the anchor table's own note that this is exactly where centuries on one Path bring an Aspect Warrior's precision level with a Space Marine's own DX. Increased HT +1 (B15, 10/level, 10) for HT 11. Increased Will +1 (B16, 5/level, 5) for Will 13, the discipline of the shrine holding Emotional Intensity firmly in check. Basic Move +2 (B17, 5/level, 10) at the user's direction, so an Aspect Warrior (Move 12) matches a Battle-Brother. 10+40+10+5+10 = 75 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 75,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_move",
							"amount": 2
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tLcLx0ulekImOH9yN",
					"name": "Enhanced Dodge",
					"reference": "B51",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Framework.md calls this out by name: superior Aeldari reflexes translate into an Enhanced Dodge for Aspect Warriors specifically, on top of Guardian-tier speed — a Dire Avenger or Howling Banshee weaving through incoming fire in a way no unaugmented human, Guardsman or Guardian, quite manages.\n\nDesign: Enhanced Dodge 1 (B51, 15 points/level).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 15,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T4RBfnbASsgMlLRMS",
			"name": "Exarch's Mastery",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What it costs, and what it grants, to be lost to the Path of the Warrior entirely: an Exarch, wearing the shrine's own war-mask and ancient armour, leading their Aspect's Aspect Warriors in battle after battle across centuries, with no path back to an ordinary life.\n\nDesign: 85 (Attribute Modifiers) + 15 (further Enhanced Dodge) + 15 (Combat Reflexes) + 30 (Trained By A Master) + 20 (Weapon Master) + 10 (Enhanced Parry 2) - 15 (Lost to the Path) = 160 points, added to the Aspect Warrior package's 249 for 409 points of physiology and mastery before skills. See the Exarch template.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tL3FEpFq8GHSLBWwI",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Exarch)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target over the Aspect Warrior + Keen Battle-Sense baseline: ST 12, DX 18, IQ 13, HT 12, Per 14 (free: IQ 13 + Keen Battle-Sense's existing +1), Will 15. Increased ST +1 (B14, 10/level, 10) for ST 12. Increased DX +2 (B15, 20/level, 40) for DX 18 — the anchor table's own figure for the single deadliest duelist tier this project has built. Increased IQ +1 (B16, 20/level, 20) for IQ 13: centuries of total focus sharpen more than reflexes. Increased HT +1 (B15, 10/level, 10) for HT 12. Increased Will +1 (B16, 5/level, 5) on top of Aspect Training's own +1, for Will 15 — an Exarch's Fanaticism-grade devotion (see Lost to the Path) needs the Will to match. 10+40+20+10+5 = 85 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 85,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tgtvjGArDow8mKeYM",
					"name": "Enhanced Dodge",
					"reference": "B51",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A further step up from an ordinary Aspect Warrior's already-formidable evasion, after centuries of nothing else.\n\nDesign: A further Enhanced Dodge 1 (B51, 15 points), stacking with Aspect Training's own level for Enhanced Dodge 2 total.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 15,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "t1vVPKe-cZxrxl9uC",
					"name": "Combat Reflexes",
					"reference": "B43",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Exarch has refought the same battle-role for centuries and simply does not freeze.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points, the same trait this project's Astartes and Ork Warboss packages use for veteran-tier battlefield composure.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 15
				},
				{
					"id": "texyawpYWQjlakJa0",
					"name": "Trained By A Master",
					"reference": "B93",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Exarch's chosen weapon-form (the shrine's own signature blade, fusion gun, or reaper launcher) is drilled to a level no ordinary Aspect Warrior reaches, matching the fiction's treatment of an Exarch as an unmatched duelist within their Aspect's own art.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Trained By A Master (B93), 30 points, one weapon-art.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 30
				},
				{
					"id": "tqDBWD4lTyILnso9C",
					"name": "Weapon Master (Aspect Weapon)",
					"reference": "B99",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See Trained By A Master, above; the two together are how GURPS models a genuine master duelist.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Weapon Master, one weapon (B99), 20 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 20
				},
				{
					"id": "tpKP4_y1mwfryaqJb",
					"name": "Enhanced Parry",
					"reference": "B51",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Centuries of the same duel, refought against every kind of foe, until the block is reflexive.\n\nDesign: Enhanced Parry 2, one weapon (B51, 5/level, 10 points).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2
				},
				{
					"id": "tjNu41G2EElcs7GYW",
					"name": "Lost to the Path (Warrior)",
					"reference": "B136",
					"local_notes": "As Fanaticism (single-minded devotion to the Path itself, here the Path of the Warrior): an Exarch cannot set the mantle down and walk away as an ordinary Aspect Warrior does when their years in the shrine end. See the top-level \"Lost to the Path\" entry above for the full design note; duplicated here as its own child so this container's point total is self-contained.\n\nLore: See the top-level \"Lost to the Path\" entry above.\n\nDesign: Fanaticism (B136, -15 points), redirected onto the Path itself; see the top-level entry above.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": -15
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TFGDXderHymYkGeFK",
			"name": "Seer's Apprenticeship",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Warlock has stepped onto the Path of the Seer far enough to touch the Runes of Battle in the middle of a fight, without (yet, or ever) being lost to it the way a Farseer is — Codex background is explicit that Warlocks remain warriors and squad leaders first, seers second.\n\nDesign: 25 points, added to the Aeldari Physiology package's 154 for 179 points of physiology before the psychic package and skills. See the Warlock template.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tH2imxF12jhWJEgxP",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Seer's Apprenticeship)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework midpoint between the Guardian baseline (IQ 12, Will 12) and the Farseer anchor (IQ 15, Will 17): a Warlock — still a battle-line fighter and squad leader, not yet fully given over to prophecy — sits partway there. Increased IQ +1 (B16, 20/level, 20) for IQ 13. Increased Will +1 (B16, 5/level, 5) for Will 14. 20+5 = 25 points. Per stays IQ-equal (13) with no extra bonus (14 only if Keen Battle-Sense is added, as the Warlock template does): a Warlock's gift runs inward, not outward, the same reasoning the Farseer anchor's own Per == IQ line shows.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 25,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T4DkedMzSROOZg1uJ",
			"name": "Farseer's Mastery",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What it costs, and what it grants, to be lost to the Path of the Seer entirely: a Farseer walks the strands of the future so far and so often that an ordinary Aeldari life — even an ordinary Warlock's life — is no longer available to them, exactly as framework.md's anchor table and Codex background both describe.\n\nDesign: 45 points, added to the Seer's Apprenticeship package's 179 for 224 points of physiology (before the Lost to the Path disadvantage, the full psychic package, and skills). See the Farseer template.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tDSbbOoxQfqIvKXUT",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Farseer)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target over the Seer's Apprenticeship baseline: IQ 15, Will 17, Per 15 (free: IQ 15 + 0, matching the anchor table's own Per == IQ line exactly). Increased IQ +2 (B16, 20/level, 40) for IQ 15 — \"psyker of the highest grade.\" Increased Will +1 (B16, 5/level, 5) on top of Seer's Apprenticeship's own +1, for Will 17: total Will bonus +2 over baseline IQ, the framework's own figure for a mind strong enough to steer the strands of fate and survive Perils of the Warp again and again across centuries. 40+5 = 45 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 45,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TI-hhBp4H-zEYs1xU",
			"name": "Autarch's Mastery",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What an Autarch actually is: not a bigger Exarch and not a Farseer with a sword, but an Aeldari who has walked several Paths far enough to master each without being lost to any of them, and who a craftworld therefore trusts to command a warhost drawn from every Aspect Shrine, Guardian defense force, and allied Path all at once.\n\nDesign: 110 (Attribute Modifiers) + 15 (further Enhanced Dodge) + 15 (Combat Reflexes) + 25 (Weapon Master) + 30 (Trained By A Master) + 5 (Enhanced Parry 1) + 10 (Charisma 2) + 15 (Reputation) + 1 (Master of Many Paths) = 226 points, added to the Aspect Warrior package's 249 for 475 points of physiology and command presence before skills. See the Autarch template, which lands above both the Exarch and Farseer totals per framework.md's own direction that an Autarch sits higher than either.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tQqLOYkxl1LbSjqAO",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Autarch)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target over the Aspect Warrior + Keen Battle-Sense baseline: ST 12, DX 18, IQ 14, HT 12, Per 15 (free: IQ 14 + Keen Battle-Sense's existing +1), Will 17 (free: IQ 14 + Aspect Training's existing +1 Will + this trait's own +2 Will, below) — set deliberately above every named anchor (Exarch's IQ 13/Will 15, Farseer's DX 14) per framework.md's own direction that an Autarch sits higher than either. Increased ST +1 (B14, 10/level, 10) for ST 12, matching an Exarch's own frame. Increased DX +2 (B15, 20/level, 40) for DX 18, matching an Exarch's own peerless reflexes rather than exceeding them — an Autarch's edge over an Exarch is breadth and command, not a faster blade. Increased IQ +2 (B16, 20/level, 40) for IQ 14: a keener strategic mind than any single-Path specialist, per Codex background's treatment of Autarchs as a craftworld's finest tacticians. Increased HT +1 (B15, 10/level, 10) for HT 12. Increased Will +2 (B16, 5/level, 10) on top of Aspect Training's own +1, for Will 17. 10+40+40+10+10 = 110 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 110,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 2
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tJ30_QFSpSoOHLbQl",
					"name": "Enhanced Dodge",
					"reference": "B51",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Autarch has fought inside enough different Aspects' own war-doctrines to match an Exarch's own evasion.\n\nDesign: A further Enhanced Dodge 1 (B51, 15 points), stacking with Aspect Training's own level for Enhanced Dodge 2 total, matching an Exarch's own tier.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 15,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tUziuQDCY9QpUz1sj",
					"name": "Combat Reflexes",
					"reference": "B43",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Autarch has led warhosts across more battles than almost any other living Aeldari.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 15
				},
				{
					"id": "tAo9H2EX_nIg21Yel",
					"name": "Weapon Master (Aspect Weapons)",
					"reference": "B99",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Unlike an Exarch, bound to one Aspect's own signature weapon-art, an Autarch has trained seriously across several — Codex background repeatedly shows Autarchs equipped with a mix-and-match loadout no single Aspect Shrine would issue.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Weapon Master, a small related group of weapons (B99), 25 points — one step above the single-weapon 20-point tier Exarch's Mastery uses.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 25
				},
				{
					"id": "tcE_8NiEXYZzwrZ-g",
					"name": "Trained By A Master",
					"reference": "B93",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Formal mastery recognized across every Aspect Shrine an Autarch has passed through on their way to the role.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Trained By A Master (B93), 30 points, matching Exarch's Mastery's own use of this trait.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 30
				},
				{
					"id": "t13gWWsrKGpT8iWGq",
					"name": "Enhanced Parry",
					"reference": "B51",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A guard drilled across multiple Aspects' own defensive doctrines.\n\nDesign: Enhanced Parry 1, one weapon group (B51, 5/level, 5 points).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tqS0cxFNJfymvu8kF",
					"name": "Charisma",
					"reference": "B41",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Autarch commands a warhost drawn from every Aspect Shrine and Guardian defense force on a craftworld, none of which owe the others any formal obedience — only genuine command presence holds it together.\n\nDesign: Charisma 2 (B41, 5/level, 10 points).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2
				},
				{
					"id": "tq7Fs63AA3BHuY9aM",
					"name": "Reputation (Legendary Autarch)",
					"reference": "B27",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Autarch's name travels between craftworlds the way a Chapter Master's does between Imperial fleets.\n\nDesign: Reputation (B27), priced in line with this project's other eyeballed Reputation entries (Ork Warboss's own Reputation, 15 points for +4).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Social",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"base_points": 15,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "reaction_bonus",
							"situation": "from Aeldari who recognise the Autarch's name and deeds, and a Fright Check-adjacent bonus/penalty for enemies who know it",
							"amount": 4
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "taFFVpAZzOS9SPhjR",
					"name": "Master of Many Paths",
					"local_notes": "Lore: What actually sets an Autarch apart from an Exarch or Farseer is this: they are not lost to any single Path. They carry what every Path taught them forward together, rather than being consumed by one — the mechanical reason this package includes no \"Lost to the Path\" disadvantage at all, unlike Exarch's Mastery and Farseer's Mastery above.\n\nDesign: A 1-point Perk (B100), +1 to any one skill-use roll per session. Homebrew, named to keep it distinct from the Basic Set Versatile advantage (B96, 5 points), which does something different.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Perk"
					],
					"base_points": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t6SZ5e0UhPUsrO0gL",
			"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
			"local_notes": "Not purchased on its own. Apply \"Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes),\n-5%\" (or the Severe variant, -10%, for the same tier of ritual/mass/\ninterstellar-scale working the human Severe variant covers) to every\nWarp Sorcery-tagged Aeldari ability below, in place of the human\nStandard (-10%) / Severe (-20%) values from Imperium/Psykers and the\nWarp.adq. Otherwise identical: same failure-margin table, same\nPushing mechanic (up to 3 pushes, cumulative -2 each).\n\nLore: Framework.md is explicit: Aeldari runecraft is far safer than unsanctioned or even Sanctioned human psychic practice, because it isn't raw, untrained talent reaching blind into the warp the way a newly-discovered human psyker's is — every Rune a Warlock or Farseer casts is shaped by millennia of accumulated craftworld runic discipline and rune-warded wargear (runes worked into armour, weapons and the spirit stone itself), refined and passed down since long before the Fall. Codex: Craftworlds background and the Path trilogy both play Aeldari psykers as controlled and precise where human psykers are volatile and dangerous even to their own side.\n\nDesign: Half the point-weight of the human variant (Standard -5% against -10%, Severe -10% against -20%), justified the same way this project's own human Perils entry justifies its Standard/Severe split (double the weight for double the stakes): rune-warding doesn't eliminate backlash risk, it roughly halves it, so the limitation's point value halves too rather than dropping to zero — an Aeldari who pushes hard enough can still trigger a Catastrophic failure, just markedly less often than an untrained human psyker rolling the same margin.",
			"tags": [
				"Reference",
				"Psyker",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tuNZs42lfGFtQTJDD",
			"name": "Aeldari Psyker (Talent)",
			"reference": "TSOR5",
			"local_notes": "Identical chassis and cost to Imperium/Psykers and the Warp.adq's\nPsyker (Talent, itself the Sorcery Talent analogue, TSOR5, 10/level):\nadds its level to Psyniscience, Meditation, Hidden Lore (the Warp),\nand the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes).\nReflavoured off the Adeptus Astra Telepathica's Imperium-specific\nAssignment scale, which doesn't apply to a species with no Black Ships\nand no Scholastia Psykana: Aeldari psychic strength is instead judged\nby how far along the Path of the Seer someone has travelled.\n  Untrained latent (every Aeldari) — Talent 0\n  Path of the Seer apprentice — Talent 1-2\n  Warlock — Talent 2-3 (still primarily a warrior and squad leader)\n  Farseer — Talent 5 (Codex background's own \"psyker of the highest grade\")\n\nLore: What actually separates a Warlock or Farseer from any other Aeldari's shared latent Psychic Sensitivity: years spent under a Seer Council's supervision, sharpening the same faculties (Psyniscience, Meditation, Hidden Lore of the Warp, and self-control against Perils) that a human Sanctioned Psyker's own Psyker Talent sharpens, before either setting the gift aside or being claimed by the Path of the Seer entirely.\n\nDesign: Talent affecting four things (three skills plus the Perils resistance roll), the same Medium Talent rate (B90, 10 points/level) Imperium's Psyker (Talent) and this project's Ork Kunnin'/Mek Instinct/Painboy's Eye all use for the same reason. Capped at level 6 for player characters, matching the Imperium trait's own cap.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1,
			"base_points": 0,
			"max_levels": 6
		},
		{
			"id": "tq3r1cApFKUiz3MF5",
			"name": "Aeldari Warp Empowerment",
			"reference": "TSOR4",
			"local_notes": "Identical chassis and cost to Imperium/Psykers and the Warp.adq's\nWarp Empowerment (itself the Sorcerous Empowerment analogue, TSOR4, 10\nbase + 10/level): the same cap rule applies unchanged — an Aeldari may\nonly know a Rune whose full, modified point cost is no greater than\nthe point cost of their own Aeldari Warp Empowerment. Requires Aeldari\nPsychic Sensitivity.\n\nRough Path-of-the-Seer mapping, worked out the same way Imperium's\nWarp Empowerment notes work out its own Assignment-grade table, from\nthis file's actual (Warp Sorcery -20% + Perils of the Warp, Aeldari\nRunes) modified costs:\n  Level      | Cap (10+10/lvl) | What the cap reaches\n  1          | 20              | most Runes of Battle basics and most single-level Runes of Fate at their starting level\n  2-3        | 30-40           | the non-attack Runes of Fate and the Runes of Battle basics (each 19 or less) with headroom\n  6          | 70              | Destructor at its full 7 dice (62) plus every other Rune of Battle — typical Warlock ceiling\n  10         | 110             | Eldritch Storm at its full 8 dice (108)\n  21         | 220             | Executioner at its full 10 dice (213): the Farseer's killing stroke — typical Farseer ceiling\nThe attack Runes (Executioner, Eldritch Storm, Destructor) are built\nat lore scale rather than party scale, so their caps are far above\nthe rest of the roster; a psyker who knows only the small Runes buys\nonly the level those need. A Warlock is far below a Farseer's\nceiling: see each template's own notes for the level it actually buys.\n\nLore: What actually gates a Rune of Battle or Rune of Fate is not raw willingness to learn it, in Codex background's own telling, but how much of the warp a given Aeldari's own training and discipline let them safely hold open at once — a Warlock's working repertoire is genuinely smaller than a Farseer's, not merely less-often used.\n\nDesign: Identical cost structure to Sorcerous Empowerment/Imperium's Warp Empowerment (10 base + 10/level): the underlying mechanic — \"how much of the warp you can safely channel at all, gating which Runes you may know by their modified cost\" — is exactly the same chassis, just judged by Path progress instead of an Imperial Assignment grade.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1,
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tBa3qMKYYeGJj7bNx",
			"name": "Aeldari Soul-Sense",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Aeldari analogue of Witch-sight: an unlearned, passive prickling awareness of psychic activity, daemonic taint and warp corruption, sharpened rather than granted outright by walking the Path of the Seer even partway.\n\nDesign: Built exactly as Imperium/Psykers and the Warp.adq's Witch-sight: Detect (Psychic Activity & Daemonic Taint), base 10 (B47-48), Warp Sorcery -20% only (no Perils: involuntary background sense, not a deliberate act). Full modified cost: 10 x 0.8 = 8 points; needs only Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mV0YD_nosgzsqZnKX",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "TuvVmTTXAAI4UVt21",
			"name": "Runes of Fate",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The oldest and most feared runes a Farseer commands: the sight to read a battle's outcome before it happens, and the will to bend that outcome once read — marking one soldier for death, guiding another's hand, or reaching directly into an enemy mind to break it.\n\nDesign: Talent-linked group; see each child. All children take Warp Sorcery (-20%) and Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes) unless noted.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "trt6OiEbq8XmJPx7K",
					"name": "Doom",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Marks a single target as fated to die in the next few moments — not a killing blow itself, but every blow against them lands truer once Doom is cast, the signature setup for a Dark Reaper volley or an Executioner-blessed strike.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level) delivering an eyeballed -25 point Vulnerability-style \"Doomed\" disadvantage (+25%, the same kind of project-valued delivered disadvantage this project's Librarius: Null Zone entry uses), Malediction (+100%, B36), Warp Sorcery (-20%) and Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net +100%. Full modified cost: 10 x 2.0 = 20 points/level; needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20), right at the cap with no headroom, marking Doom as a Farseer's signature opening rune rather than something learned lightly.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m16WqJgEr52mctJdY",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Doomed",
							"cost_adj": "+25%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mstmAfRJLwbQxQE3v",
							"name": "Malediction 1",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mUIWzdgDH5AlLnvxm",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "muQyrz45pReJAQcZC",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
							"cost_adj": "-5%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 10,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tKGZ5-OucpNoDzNf8",
					"name": "Guide",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Doom's twin and opposite: guides a chosen ally's next strike straight and true, the Farseer's own hand steadying theirs from a distance.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level) delivering a +25 point \"Guided\" combat advantage to a willing recipient (Basic B35 allows either an Advantage or a Disadvantage Delivered), Malediction (+100%, used here for its \"affects anyone you can see, no attack roll\" reach rather than its resistance clause, since the target volunteers), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Granting an advantage costs +10% per point it is worth (B36), ten times the rate for inflicting a disadvantage, so the 25 points are +250% and the net is +325%. Full modified cost: 10 x 4.25 = 42.5, rounded up to 43 points; needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 4 (cap 50). Doom's mirror in effect, at twice its price.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mgXVRd__tGSvKRo5Y",
							"name": "Advantage Delivered (Guided",
							"cost_adj": "+250%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mEQPhg0RijV5th_b2",
							"name": "Malediction 1",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mwF0GAGrPtXftVyFh",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mcgW2C-qVv2XtbhKJ",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
							"cost_adj": "-5%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 10,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "t3dwcmerGff3QLHay",
					"name": "Fortune",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A ward cast over a squad that lets one failed save, in the following moments, be quietly rerolled — the same kind of battlefield luck this project's Sanctic Daemonology: Sanctuary and Librarius: Might of Heroes entries deliver to Imperial squads, reflavoured as the Farseer's own gift of fortune.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a +15 point Luck-tier advantage to willing recipients, Area Effect (+50%, B102, 2-yard radius), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, Severe, -10%, the same tier this project's own ritual/squad-scale workings use). The advantage is +10% per point (B36), +150%. Net +170%. Full modified cost: 10 x 2.7 = 27 points; needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "muk04LKyDMzKN5UTF",
							"name": "Advantage Delivered (Fortune's Ward",
							"cost_adj": "+150%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m8RTSrTnfrw-_Rkkd",
							"name": "Area Effect",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "modh0dKpYb4HQJkbB",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mF-OnpMfMrJ_7n8o0",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes, Severe)",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tgUggra_p0rWGxG87",
					"name": "Executioner",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The psychic blade that slays its target outright: on the tabletop the Executioner inflicts mortal wounds that no armour or ward turns aside, and most often it is called on a target already Doomed. Here it is a killing stroke that ignores armour almost entirely.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Impaling, 5/die, B61) bought at 10 levels, 10d(10) imp, with Malediction 2 (+150%, B106; resisted by Will, not dodged, with the normal Size and Speed/Range penalties, so it reaches its lore range of 18-24 inches), Armor Divisor (10) (+200%, B102), Warp Sorcery (-20%) and Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net +325%. Per level: 5 x (1 + 1.5 + 2 - 0.20 - 0.05) = 21.25; full modified cost 212.5, rounded up to 213; needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 21 (cap 220). Scale check: 10d(10) averages 35 before armour. A Battle-Brother (torso DR 103, effective 10.3) takes about 25 penetrating x2 = 49 injury against HP 34; a Guardian (flak 30, effective 3) about 64 against HP 11; a Carnifex (DR 150, effective 15, then Damage Reduction 3) about 20 x2 / 3 = 13 against HP 70, so it survives one hit that a Battle-Brother or Guardian does not. A lesser psyker may buy fewer levels; the template buys the full 10.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mAfDlK9dR1UQMSVyB",
							"name": "Malediction 2",
							"cost_adj": "+150%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mdX-3RLohkj8by8mk",
							"name": "Armor Divisor (10)",
							"cost_adj": "+200%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mdfqp9AjGGiUNMclF",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mONQc069sp72pbZri",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
							"cost_adj": "-5%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tCGifnDyo4uJmCluz",
					"name": "Eldritch Storm",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A tearing storm of raw warp-force thrown out over a wide killing ground — a Farseer's answer to a stalled advance or a densely packed enemy line.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Crushing, 5/die) bought at 8 levels, 8d(2) cr ex, with Explosion at the 8-yard tier (+150%, B106), Armor Divisor (2) (+50%, B102), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, Severe, -10%, matching this project's own area-bombardment tier precedent). Net +170%. Per level: 5 x 2.7 = 13.5; full modified cost 108; needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 10 (cap 110). A lesser psyker may buy fewer levels; the template buys all 8.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m90of3Q6M2YQyhyGr",
							"name": "Explosion",
							"cost_adj": "+150%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mRaTEnoVdnaqnsjca",
							"name": "Armor Divisor (2)",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "maX0z11by1fbDcAXL",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mNOp2-KVuM3t7q57k",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes, Severe)",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 8
				},
				{
					"id": "txMaS0A8DnLC3Maug",
					"name": "Mind War",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A direct psychic duel: the Farseer's own force of will bears down on an enemy mind until it breaks, no visible attack for the target to dodge or block.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level) delivering mental/FP damage, Based on Will (+20%, B102, the attack is a battle of wills rather than a straight HT roll), Malediction (+100%), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net +95%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.95 = 19.5, rounded up to 20 points; needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20), the discipline's other cap-tight signature rune alongside Doom.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
